WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.812
How do you know it's least privilege?

2
00:00:01.812 --> 00:00:06.504
The guide's Validate for Step 6: from a
pilot device off the corporate network,

3
00:00:06.504 --> 00:00:11.270
reach the application on its port, and
confirm that a port outside the segment

4
00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:15.887
fails; the client's Policy tester shows
which rule handles the destination.

5
00:00:15.887 --> 00:00:19.852
The app's policy runs in
report-only for five business days,

6
00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:22.825
read in the sign-in log's
report-only results.

7
00:00:22.825 --> 00:00:26.217
Enforcement sets the policy
on, adds ring groups,

8
00:00:26.217 --> 00:00:31.475
and then turns off the V P N route for
that application, which Module 6 covers.

9
00:00:31.475 --> 00:00:36.745
Rollback removes the group's assignment,
or puts the policy back in report-only,

10
00:00:36.745 --> 00:00:39.663
and the V P N route stays
until the wave holds.

11
00:00:39.663 --> 00:00:43.987
On day two, the application owner
reviews the assignment each quarter,

12
00:00:43.987 --> 00:00:48.237
as an access review, and the platform
owner keeps at least two healthy,

13
00:00:48.237 --> 00:00:50.101
current connectors per group.

14
00:00:50.101 --> 00:00:54.754
The metric is the Quick Access
residual: segments left in Quick Access,

15
00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:57.563
and apps without an
assignment or a policy.

16
00:00:57.563 --> 00:01:00.120
The starting target for both is zero.
